  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Legal and institutional reforms initiated to promote the enabling environment for sustainable enterprises</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Albania&#x2019;s private sector is a key driver of economic growth but has yet to fully embrace sustainable business practices. As the country moves toward EU integration, upgrading business models and aligning with EU standards is essential. The ILO focuses on two priority sectors: textile, clothing, leather, and footwear (TCLF) and tourism. 

In the tourism sector, the ILO works to address informality by piloting incentives for enterprise formalization. 

In TCLF, enterprises face challenges in job quality, working conditions, productivity, and environmental management. The ILO supports businesses through the Sustaining Competitive and Responsible Enterprises (SCORE) program, helping companies improve working conditions, enhance competitiveness and productivity, and adopt sustainable practices. This includes strengthening Employers&#x2019; and Workers&#x2019; organisations operating in the sector and training of the Labour Inspectorate on enforcing occupational safety and health standards. 

These efforts, implemented in collaboration with IndustriALL and EURATEX, aim to create a more sustainable, competitive, and responsible private sector in Albania.</narrative>
  </description>
